  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "According to Toyota, what is the part number for the oil filter cap assembly for the highest MSRP 2020 Toyota SUV that uses a battery with the same chemistry as the 2021 Toyota Aqua?",
  "answer": "**Answer: 15620-36020**\n\n## Research Summary\n\n### Step 1: 2021 Toyota Aqua Battery Chemistry\nThe 2021 Toyota Aqua (second generation, XP210) uses **bipolar nickel-metal hydride (NiMH) battery** for most trim grades (X, G, Z, GR Sport). This was confirmed by Toyota's official July 2021 press release stating \"world's first vehicle to use a high-output bipolar nickel-hydrogen battery\" and Toyota Industries' confirmation of \"bipolar nickel-metal hydride batteries for hybrid vehicles... production for the Toyota Aqua beginning May 2021\" [1][2].\n\n### Step 2: 2020 Toyota SUVs with Same NiMH Chemistry\nThe 2020 Toyota SUVs using NiMH (matching the Aqua's chemistry):\n- **2020 Toyota Highlander Hybrid** — NiMH confirmed by Green Car Reports\n- **2020 Toyota RAV4 Hybrid** — Base/most trims use NiMH\n- **2020 Toyota C-HR Hybrid** — NiMH\n- **2020 Toyota Corolla Cross Hybrid** — NiMH\n\nThe 2020 Toyota Venza uses **Lithium-Ion** and does NOT share the chemistry [3].\n\n### Step 3: Highest MSRP 2020 Toyota Hybrid SUV\n| Model | Top Trim | MSRP |\n|-------|----------|------|\n| RAV4 Hybrid | Limited AWD | $38,055 |\n| **Highlander Hybrid** | **Platinum AWD** | **$50,200** |\n\n**2020 Toyota Highlander Hybrid Platinum AWD at $50,200** is the highest MSRP [4].\n\n### Step 4: Oil Filter Cap Assembly Part Number\nFor the **2020 Toyota Highlander Hybrid (2.5L A25A-FXS hybrid engine)**, the Toyota OEM oil filter cap assembly part number is **15620-36020** (supersedes 15620-36010 and 15620-0V010) [5][6][7].\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] https://global.toyota/en/newsroom/corporate/35971839.html — Toyota official press release: \"world's first vehicle to use a high-output bipolar nickel-hydrogen battery\"\n\n[2] https://www.toyota-industries.com/products/automobile/batteries/index.html — Toyota Industries: \"Bipolar nickel-metal hydride batteries for hybrid vehicles... production for the Toyota Aqua beginning at the Kyowa Plant in May 2021\"\n\n[3] https://www.greencarreports.com/news/1124637_2020-toyota-highlander-hybrid-gets-more-power-nimh-battery — Green Car Reports: \"The Highlander continues Toyota's commitment to nickel-metal hydride over lithium-ion\"\n\n[4] https://www.cargurus.com/Cars/2020-Toyota-Highlander-Hybrid-Prices-c24108 — CarGurus historical pricing showing Platinum AWD at $50,200 MSRP\n\n[5] https://parts.lakelandtoyota.com/p/TOYOTA_2020_HIGHLANDER-Hybrid-XLE/Filter-Oil-Cap-Cover-Housing/3898369/1562036020.html — Lakeland Toyota parts catalog: 2020 Highlander Hybrid 2.5L Hybrid fitment for 1562036020\n\n[6] https://parts.woburntoyota.com/p/Toyota_2020_Highlander/Filter-Oil-Cap-Cover-Housing/48067404/1562036020.html — Woburn Toyota parts catalog: 2020 Highlander 2.5L Hybrid fitment for 1562036020\n\n[7] https://parts.toyota.com/p/Toyota_2018_/CAP-ASSEMBLY---OIL-FILTER/62914430/1562036020.html — Official Toyota parts site listing 15620-36020 as \"Oil Filter Cap Assembly\"",
